    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This Capstone thesis addresses historical and cultural narratives of the South Caucasus region through the lens of the Transcaucasian Trail (TCT) project, a long-distance hiking trail across the Southern Caucasus which fuses wayfaring cartographic traditions and modern mapping technologies. By following a written wayfare of the northeastern section of the trail running through Azerbaijan, this work aims to dispel stereotypes of the Caucasus through illustrating how the movement of peoples and ideas has continuously reshaped the region. The Caucasus is revealed as a dynamic space, enriched by centuries of exchange both within and beyond its borders, through exploration of the Taj Mahal mosque in Aniq village, and an ancient transhumance route crossing the depths of the mountains.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Garibova, N. (2024). Wayfaring the Caucasus: Re-envisioning the Region through the Movements that Shaped it. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/zx207wz6049. https://doi.org/10.25740/zx207wz6049.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
